{"name":"High Risk Red","hex":"#c71f2d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"high","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Physically elevated, extending above a base or average level:\n Very elevated; extending or being far above a base; tall; lofty.","Very elevated; extending or being far above a base; tall; lofty."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["In or to an elevated position.","In or at a great value."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/high"},{"term":"risk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The probability of a negative outcome to a decision or event.","The magnitude of possible loss consequent to a decision or event."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To incur risk of (an unwanted or negative outcome).","To incur risk of harming or jeopardizing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/risk"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Risk","blocks":[{"text":"Risk is the possibility of something bad happening, comprising a level of uncertainty about the effects and implications of an activity, particularly negative and undesirable consequences."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/3_Alarm_Building_Fire.jpg/330px-3_Alarm_Building_Fire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Risk","wikidata":"Q104493"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Milwaukee_Harbor_sign_5892.jpg/500px-Milwaukee_Harbor_sign_5892.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Milwaukee_Harbor_sign_5892.jpg/1280px-Milwaukee_Harbor_sign_5892.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Milwaukee_Harbor_sign_5892.jpg/500px-Milwaukee_Harbor_sign_5892.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Harbor sign warning visitors that use of the walkway is \"at your own risk\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMilwaukee_Harbor_sign_5892.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Impact_event.jpg/500px-Impact_event.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Impact_event.jpg/500px-Impact_event.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Artist's impression of a major asteroid impact, an example of a global catastrophic risk.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fil